{
  "id": "web-dev-059",
  "title": "Most Commonly Used Tags in HTML - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>HTML tags are the fundamental building blocks of </span><a href=\"#/article/distributed-systems/distributed-systems-108\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>web development,</span></a><span> providing the structure and organization necessary for creating web pages.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>They include tags for headings, paragraphs, links, images, and more.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Commonly used tags like &lt;html&gt;, &lt;head&gt;, and &lt;body&gt; are essential for creating a well-structured web document.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>These tags provide the framework for building user-friendly and accessible </span><a href=\"#/article/networking/networking-201\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>web pages.</span></a></li></ul><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">index.html</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">h1</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Welcome to My Website<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">h1</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">p</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>This is a paragraph introducing the content of my website.<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">p</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">a</span> <span class=\"na\">href</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Visit GeeksforGeeks<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">a</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The &lt;h1&gt; tag defines a top-level heading, which serves as the main title of the webpage.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1713\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>&lt;p&gt; tag</span></a><span> defines a paragraph, providing a block of text to introduce the website's content.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>The</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1679\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span> &lt;a&gt; tag</span></a><span> defines a hyperlink, allowing users to navigate to another webpage, in this case, \"</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1714\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/</span></a><span>\".</span></li></ul><h2 id=\"document-structure-tag\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>Document structure tag</strong></b></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The &lt;html&gt; tag is essential, encapsulating the entire HTML document and serving as the root element for content organization.</span></p><table><thead><tr><th style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Structure Tag</span></th><th style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Syntax</span></th><th style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Description</span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1709\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;html&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;html&gt; Statements... &lt;/html&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>The root of the HTML document specifies it as HTML.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1675\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;head&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;head&gt; Statements... &lt;/head&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Contains head elements such as title, style, and meta tags in the HTML file.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1715\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;title&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;title&gt; Statements... &lt;/title&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines the title of an HTML document.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1676\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;body&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;body&gt; Statements... &lt;/body&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines the body of an HTML document, containing content like images, tables, and lists.</span></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id=\"commonly-used-tags-in-html\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Commonly used tags in HTML</span></h2><table><thead><tr><th style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>HTML Tag</span></th><th style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Syntax</span></th><th style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Description</span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1681\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;div&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;div&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines a division or section in an HTML document.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1678\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;p&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;p&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines a paragraph.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1679\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;a&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;a href=\"...\"&gt;...&lt;/a&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines a hyperlink.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1716\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;img&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;img src=\"...\" alt=\"...\"&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Embeds an image.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-069\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;ul&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;...&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines an unordered list.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1717\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;ol&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;...&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines an ordered list.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1680\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;li&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;li&gt;...&lt;/li&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines a list item.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-061\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;table&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;table&gt;...&lt;/table&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines a table.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-062\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;tr&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;tr&gt;...&lt;/tr&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines a table row.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-063\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;th&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;th&gt;...&lt;/th&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines a table header cell.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-064\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;td&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;td&gt;...&lt;/td&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines a table data cell.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-081\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;form&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;form&gt;...&lt;/form&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines an HTML form for user input.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-082\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;input&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;input type=\"...\"&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines an input control within a form.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1672\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;button&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;button&gt;...&lt;/button&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines a clickable button.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1677\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;h1&gt;</span></code><span>-</span><code><span>&lt;h6&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;h1&gt;...&lt;/h1&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Define headings of different levels.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1718\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;span&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;span&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines a generic inline container.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-083\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;label&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;label for=\"...\"&gt;...&lt;/label&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Defines a label for an input element.</span></td></tr><tr><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-091\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><code><span>&lt;iframe&gt;</span></code></a></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><code><span>&lt;iframe src=\"...\"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;</span></code></td><td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span>Embeds an inline frame for external content.</span></td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id=\"use-of-basic-html-structure-tags\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Use of Basic HTML Structure Tags</span></h3><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">index.html</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">head</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">title</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>My First Web Page<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">title</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">head</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">h1</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Welcome to My Website<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">h1</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The</span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1709\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span> &lt;html&gt; tag</span></a><span> defines the root element of the HTML document, encompassing all content.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1675\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>&lt;head&gt;</span></a><span> tag contains meta-information about the document, such as its title.</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1676\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>&lt;body&gt;</span></a><span> tag includes all visible content displayed on the webpage.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"styling-text-with-html-tags\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Styling Text with HTML Tags</span></h3><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">index.html</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">h1</span> <span class=\"na\">style</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"color: green;\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Welcome to Geeks for Geeks<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">h1</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">p</span> <span class=\"na\">style</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"font-size: 16px;\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Geeks for Geeks is a computer science portal for geeks.<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">p</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">a</span> <span class=\"na\">href</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/\"</span> <span class=\"na\">style</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"text-decoration: none; color: blue;\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n      Visit Geeks for Geeks<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">a</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The &lt;p&gt; tag defines a paragraph with a font size of 16px, providing a brief description.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>The &lt;a&gt; tag creates a hyperlink with blue text and no underline, directing users to the Geeks for Geeks website.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"creating-a-course-list-with-html-tags\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Creating a Course List with HTML Tags</span></h3><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">index.html</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">h2</span> <span class=\"na\">style</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Available Courses<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">h2</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">ul</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n        <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Web Development<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n        <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Data Structures<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n        <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Machine Learning<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">li</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">ul</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The &lt;h2&gt; tag creates a subheading with a specified font family, titled \"Available Courses.\"</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>The &lt;ul&gt; tag defines an unordered list, and &lt;li&gt; tags represent individual list items, each naming a course.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"best-practices-for-commonly-used-html-tags\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Best Practices for Commonly Used HTML Tags</span></h3><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Implementing best practices when using HTML tags ensures your web content is well-structured, accessible, and SEO-friendly. Here are key guidelines to consider:</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong>Use Semantic Tags</strong></b><span>: Employ tags like </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1719\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>&lt;header&gt;,</span></a><span> </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1720\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>&lt;nav&gt;</span></a><span>, </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1721\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>&lt;article&gt;</span></a><span>, and </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1722\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>&lt;footer&gt;</span></a><span> to clearly define the structure of your content, enhancing readability and </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1710\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>SEO.</span></a><span> </span></li><li value=\"3\"><b><strong>Ensure Proper Nesting</strong></b><span>: Maintain correct nesting of tags to prevent rendering issues and ensure the document adheres to HTML standards. </span></li><li value=\"4\"><b><strong>Use Anchor Text in Links</strong></b><span>: Use clear and descriptive text within </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1723\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>&lt;a&gt; tags</span></a><span> to inform users and search engines about the linked content. </span></li></ul></div>",
  "textContent": "HTML tags are the fundamental building blocks of web development, providing the structure and organization necessary for creating web pages.They include tags for headings, paragraphs, links, images, and more.Commonly used tags like <html>, <head>, and <body> are essential for creating a well-structured web document.These tags provide the framework for building user-friendly and accessible web pages.\n            index.html\n\n    <!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<body>\n    <h1>Welcome to My Website</h1>\n    <p>This is a paragraph introducing the content of my website.</p>\n    <a href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/\">Visit GeeksforGeeks</a>\n</body>\n</html>\n\nThe <h1> tag defines a top-level heading, which serves as the main title of the webpage.The <p> tag defines a paragraph, providing a block of text to introduce the website's content.The <a> tag defines a hyperlink, allowing users to navigate to another webpage, in this case, \"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/\".Document structure tagThe <html> tag is essential, encapsulating the entire HTML document and serving as the root element for content organization.Structure TagSyntaxDescription<html><html> Statements... </html>The root of the HTML document specifies it as HTML.<head><head> Statements... </head>Contains head elements such as title, style, and meta tags in the HTML file.<title><title> Statements... </title>Defines the title of an HTML document.<body><body> Statements... </body>Defines the body of an HTML document, containing content like images, tables, and lists.Commonly used tags in HTMLHTML TagSyntaxDescription<div><div>...</div>Defines a division or section in an HTML document.<p><p>...</p>Defines a paragraph.<a><a href=\"...\">...</a>Defines a hyperlink.<img><img src=\"...\" alt=\"...\">Embeds an image.<ul><ul><li>...</li></ul>Defines an unordered list.<ol><ol><li>...</li></ol>Defines an ordered list.<li><li>...</li>Defines a list item.<table><table>...</table>Defines a table.<tr><tr>...</tr>Defines a table row.<th><th>...</th>Defines a table header cell.<td><td>...</td>Defines a table data cell.<form><form>...</form>Defines an HTML form for user input.<input><input type=\"...\">Defines an input control within a form.<button><button>...</button>Defines a clickable button.<h1>-<h6><h1>...</h1>Define headings of different levels.<span><span>...</span>Defines a generic inline container.<label><label for=\"...\">...</label>Defines a label for an input element.<iframe><iframe src=\"...\"></iframe>Embeds an inline frame for external content.Use of Basic HTML Structure Tags\n            index.html\n\n    <!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n    <title>My First Web Page</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <h1>Welcome to My Website</h1>\n</body>\n</html>\n\nThe <html> tag defines the root element of the HTML document, encompassing all content.The <head> tag contains meta-information about the document, such as its title.The <body> tag includes all visible content displayed on the webpage.Styling Text with HTML Tags\n            index.html\n\n    <!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<body>\n    <h1 style=\"color: green;\">Welcome to Geeks for Geeks</h1>\n    <p style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Geeks for Geeks is a computer science portal for geeks.</p>\n    <a href=\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/\" style=\"text-decoration: none; color: blue;\">\n      Visit Geeks for Geeks</a>\n</body>\n</html>\n\nThe <p> tag defines a paragraph with a font size of 16px, providing a brief description.The <a> tag creates a hyperlink with blue text and no underline, directing users to the Geeks for Geeks website.Creating a Course List with HTML Tags\n            index.html\n\n    <!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<body>\n    <h2 style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\">Available Courses</h2>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Web Development</li>\n        <li>Data Structures</li>\n        <li>Machine Learning</li>\n    </ul>\n</body>\n</html>\n\nThe <h2> tag creates a subheading with a specified font family, titled \"Available Courses.\"The <ul> tag defines an unordered list, and <li> tags represent individual list items, each naming a course.Best Practices for Commonly Used HTML TagsImplementing best practices when using HTML tags ensures your web content is well-structured, accessible, and SEO-friendly. Here are key guidelines to consider:Use Semantic Tags: Employ tags like <header>, <nav>, <article>, and <footer> to clearly define the structure of your content, enhancing readability and SEO. Ensure Proper Nesting: Maintain correct nesting of tags to prevent rendering issues and ensure the document adheres to HTML standards. Use Anchor Text in Links: Use clear and descriptive text within <a> tags to inform users and search engines about the linked content.",
  "url": "https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/html/most-commonly-used-tags-in-html"
}
